# width: 120
# height: 40
# The right end of the bottom row: `⟳  … running…` while async HTTP work
# is in flight, and a click on it aborts. A toast fades in three seconds
# and a bench does not, so without the indicator a long op has no signal
# at all once its toast has gone.

# `serve 0`: the runner binds a free port before the file starts and
# `${SERVE_PORT}` names it — a fixed port collided when two runs of the
# corpus shared a machine.
serve 0 200 delay=20000 "late"
write slow.http "GET http://127.0.0.1:${SERVE_PORT}/slow\n"
open slow.http

command http.send
wait 500
expect screen contains "running…"

# The indicator is the click target, right-aligned one cell off the edge.
click 112 39
# // changed (edge-grip): off the row again — resting on it is what
# summons the launcher dock, which would paint over the echo below.
hover 60 10
expect screen contains "http.abort: cancelled"
expect screen lacks "running…"
